## LOGICA Website QA Checklist

## Accessibility and Keyboard navigation
- [ ] The pages should be traversed in order using 'Tab' and 'Shift+Tab'.
- [ ] Every can be focused using keyboard navigation.
- [ ] Images such as board member profiles should include meaningful 'alt' text, default images should also have its appropiate text.

## 1. Landing Page
- [ ] Page header displays their associated content.
- [ ] Navigation elements take the visitor to other sections of the page.
- [ ] Event and other links takes the visitor to the relevent page.
- [ ] Event calendar displays upcoming events to the visitor.
    - Empty state: if there is no events or content to be shown, it displays basic information, mission, and navigation.
- [ ] Loading state: Display a loading indicator if the content is being updated and shown to the visitor from the backend.
- [ ] Error State: Clear error message and retry if data fails to fetch from `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`.

## 2. Team/Role Pages
- [ ] Board member cards display the member's photo along with their name and role.
- [ ] Page header displays their associated content.
- [ ] Content links such as Linkedin, should take the visitor to the relevant page.
- [ ] Board member cards display photo, name, and role.
    - Empty state: If there is no content to be shown for the board member. Display a message indicating that the content and information will come soon, along with default profile placeholder. 
- [ ] The visitor can navigate to other pages using the navigation element.

## 3. Sign-in screen + session/role check
- [ ] Email fields should only accept @email inputs.
- [ ] Visitor should be able to request a new verification code that is acceptable to verify.
- [ ] Verification should be able to render invalid if the code is invalid or expired.
- [ ] User's membership corresponds to their current role.
- [ ] Members have access to member-only content.
- [ ] Other roles should see their own content appropiate to their role.
- [ ] Signing out required the user to log in again.
- [ ] Empty State: If user is not signed in, do not display members-only content and request authentication.
- [ ] Error State:
    - [ ] Email input accepts only @email type and @uic.edu.
    - [ ] Verification should display invalid and expired code seperately.
    - [ ] User is able to fail authentication.
    - [ ] Sign in sessions should expire if left idle for a certain amount of time.
    - [ ] Unauthorized access should display a message for members who don't have access.

